From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:07:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 101/342] meson_gpio and gpio: the ODROID-C2's header pins as
 GPIO

/dev/misc/gpio reads as a table of the 40-pin header's GPIO pins (the
SoC pin, its function, direction, level, pull) and takes "<pin> out
0|1", "<pin> in [up|down|none]" and "<pin> release", by header pin
number or SoC pin name. Making a pin GPIO clears the mux bits of its
alternate functions; the first command saves the pin's bits for release.
Only header pins are offered, and the I2C pins only while I2C isn't
selected (I2C A carries the RTC shield). The "gpio" command wraps it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
